# Cloudberry's singlenode_regress suite, as the port runs it: every test of
# its two schedules, in their order, with what the port does with it.
#
#   run   the test runs here, against every M1 module and gp_ao, M5's.  A
#         third word names the group it runs in, which is its first group
#         when there is none: PostgreSQL's tests run first, and then each
#         group of Cloudberry's on a copy of the server they leave, the
#         groups side by side, each in this order.  The groups are cut by
#         ORCA's time, in the order of the tests, so that a test still
#         follows the ones it followed.
#   pg    one of PostgreSQL's own regression tests, in Cloudberry's copy of
#         it for PostgreSQL 14; the pgregress suite runs PostgreSQL 19's
#   skip  it needs what the port does not have, which the rest of the line
#         says
#
# A test in a directory is named with it, uao_compaction/basic; one that
# Cloudberry's pg_regress makes twice from one file, for a row-oriented and a
# column-oriented table, is named as it names the two, uao_dml/..._row and
# uao_dml/..._column.
